The same columns in another order: the table is rebuilt, and each value is
copied by its column's name, not its place.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, note TEXT) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup', 'hot');

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, note TEXT, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, 4 steps
  table `dish`: aside, to make it anew
    ALTER TABLE "dish" RENAME TO "roux_old_dish"
  table `dish`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, note TEXT, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT
  table `dish`: its rows, by id, name, note
    INSERT INTO "dish" ("id", "name", "note") SELECT "id", "name", "note" FROM "roux_old_dish"
  table `dish`: the old one
    DROP TABLE "roux_old_dish"
